# Laziness proof: an unused dict entry is never forced, even if it contains a raise.
# Dict entries are thunks — evaluation is deferred until the value is accessed.
# [result: used] only accesses `used`, so `unused` is never forced and the raise
# never fires.
[unused: [raise "dead binding remains lazy"]  used: 42]
[result: used]
=== error
[E080] dead binding remains lazy (defined at stdlib/prelude.llt:2496:28-2496:47)
  --> stdlib/prelude.llt:2496:28-2496:47
   |
  2496 | """]: [fn [let msg@String] [builtin-raise msg]]
       |                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  in [builtin-raise ...] at stdlib/prelude.llt:2496:28-2496:47
   |
  2496 | """]: [fn [let msg@String] [builtin-raise msg]]
       |                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  in materialized at 4:1-4:56
